Ukraine's allies announced additional air defence support for Kyiv at a summit in Paris on Monday, along with exercises for the forces that will be deployed after a ceasefire, as part of efforts to increase pressure on Russia to end the war.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/bf21afce-7f01-11f1-af6d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-13T163612Z-1269730039-RC24DMAN3E13-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-COALITION-FRANCE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/bf21afce-7f01-11f1-af6d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-13T163612Z-1269730039-RC24DMAN3E13-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-COALITION-FRANCE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3fd490d0-7f5e-11f1-b426-45e43ba2eff1</guid><pubDate>Tue, 14 Jul 2026 09:40:49 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/bf21afce-7f01-11f1-af6d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-13T163612Z-1269730039-RC24DMAN3E13-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-COALITION-FRANCE.jpg">via REUTERS - Teresa Suarez</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Expanded World Cup delivers as Infantino eyes 64 teams next</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260714-fifa-chief-infantino-hints-at-64-team-world-cup-world-cup-2026</link><description>
Bosses at World Cup organisers Fifa have revealed they are considering the expansion of the competition from 48 to 64 teams.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d64e256e-6508-11f1-9587-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP22329467097755.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d64e256e-6508-11f1-9587-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP22329467097755.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7a0c4a28-7ee0-11f1-beb0-a5f5c3bb5b6a</guid><pubDate>Tue, 14 Jul 2026 12:46:30 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d64e256e-6508-11f1-9587-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP22329467097755.jpg">AP - Hassan Ammar</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Ethiopia 'closely engaged' over citizens facing execution in Saudi Arabia</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260714-ethiopia-closely-engaged-over-citizens-facing-execution-in-saudi-arabia</link><description>
Ethiopia says it's continuing "sustained diplomatic and consular efforts" to help dozens of its citizens facing the death penalty in Saudi Arabia, after an international rights group warned that at least 58 Ethiopian migrants are at imminent risk of execution.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0484b668-7f7c-11f1-be68-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP20043577409446.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0484b668-7f7c-11f1-be68-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP20043577409446.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f14d2d7a-7f74-11f1-b090-5797132e4456</guid><pubDate>Tue, 14 Jul 2026 13:43:25 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0484b668-7f7c-11f1-be68-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP20043577409446.jpg">AP - Nariman El-Mofty</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Paris balls cancelled amid heatwave as France marks 10 years since Nice attack</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260713-bastille-day-events-disrupted-by-heat-as-france-marks-nice-attack-anniversary</link><description>
Bastille Day firefighters' balls in Paris and the surrounding suburbs have been cancelled owing to record high temperatures affecting the capital and most of France, as emergency workers remain on alert. Celebrations begin on Monday, with Paris having brought forward its annual fireworks display by a day to avoid clashing with commemorations marking the 10th anniversary of the Nice attack of 14 July, 2016.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9cd2df1e-7e12-11f1-b372-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9QV9AD.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9cd2df1e-7e12-11f1-b372-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9QV9AD.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1e326d98-7eb5-11f1-8c6f-fb9125324903</guid><pubDate>Mon, 13 Jul 2026 17:25:45 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9cd2df1e-7e12-11f1-b372-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9QV9AD.jpg">© Dimitar Dilkoff/AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>France, Germany, UK condemn Iran attacks as renewed fighting with US puts peace deal at risk</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260713-france-germany-uk-condemn-iran-attacks-as-renewed-fighting-with-us-puts-peace-deal-at-risk</link><description>
The foreign ministers of France, Germany, and Britain have condemned Iran's attacks on shipping in the Strait of Hormuz and on countries in the region, as Iran and the United States have traded attacks in recent days, casting doubt on their interim agreement to end the war.
